SECTION 2

INTERPRETATION

Unless otherwise stated herein:

(a) "ILORIN EMIRATE" covers and includes the following Towns and Districts:

(i)     Ilorin Town;

(ii)    Iponrin District;

(iii)   Afon District;

(iv)    Malete District;

(v)     Akanbi District;

(vi)    Ejidongari District;

(vii)   Oloru District;

(viii) Owode District;

(ix)    Onire District;

(x)     Lanwa District and

(xi)    Ipaiye District.



Now comprising Asa, Ilorin East, Ilorin South, Ilorin West and Moro Local Government Areas
of Kwara State.

(b)

        (i)     "UNION" means ILORIN EMIRATE DESCENDANTS PROGRESSIVE
                UNION,

        (ii)    "MEMBER" means a registered financial member of the Union.

        (iii)   "EXECUTIVE MEMBER" means member of any Executive arm of the Union.


       (iv)   "INDIGENE" means a DESCENDANT OF ILORIN EMIRATE as defined
              above.

       (v)    "WARD" means a traditional title area within Ilorin.

       (vi)   "BANK" refers to any legally recognized Bank in Nigeria wherein the Union
              maintains account(s).

SECTION 3

AIMS AND OBJECTIVES

The aims and objectives of the Union shall be to:

(a)    Foster and promote unity, progress and mutual. understanding amongst the indigenes of
       Ilorin Emirate and other communities;

(b)    Co-operate/collaborate with other similar Unions/Associations/Institutions within the
       State and other parts of the Federation for mutual benefit.

(c)    Honour and show appreciation for individuals'/group'-outstanding contributions towards
       the development of the community;

(d)    Promote the socio-economic, cultural and educational development of the Community;

(e)    Promote security and welfare of its members and the wellbeing of the entire Ilorin
       Community;

(f)    Publish books and periodicals on the activities of the Union;

(g)    Co-operate and work with various Islamic religious groups within the Community with a
       view to propagating Islam;

(h)    Acquire and own property(ies) in furtherance of the objectives of the Union;

(i)    Collate, project and represent the views and stand of the Community on developmental
       issues; and

(j)    Do all such other lawful things that will enable the Union attain its objectives.

SECTION 6

(a) ORGANISATIONAL STRUCTURE OF THE UNION

         The Organs of the Union shall be:

(i)      National Conferences

(ii)     National Executive Council

(iii)    Zone

(iv)     Branch



(b)      COMPOSITION, CONDITIONS AND FUNCTIONS OF THE ORGANS OF THE
         UNION

       (i) NATIONAL CONFERENCES


       1) The National Conference shall be the highest organ of the Union and its decisions shall
          be final;
       2) The Union shall hold Annual National Conference to which accredited Branches shall be
          required to send delegates;
       3) National Conference membership shall comprise the accredited delegates from Branches
          and current members of the National Executive Council;
       4) A Branch delegation shall comprise at least one member and at most four members of the
          Branch;
       5) The Annual Conference shall be held over at least two succeeding days during the month
          of December in Ilorin Emirate at a Venue as may be decided by the National Executive
          Council;
       6) The Branches shall be informed of the date of the Conference at least two months before
          its commencement;
       7) On the days of the Annual Conference, members shall receive Annual Reports for the
          current year's activities of the Union together with audited Statement of Accounts;
       8) An emergency National Conference may be summoned by the National Executive
          Council if and when circumstances demand;
       9) The quorum of the National Conference shall be two third (2/3) of the number of
          accredited Branches of the Union;
       10) Two third (2/3) registered Branches shall have the power to summon an Emergency
          National Conference if and when circumstances demand.



(ii)      NATIONAL EXECUTIVE COUNCIL

It shall be the duty of the National Executive Council (NEC) to:

(1)       Defend the Constitution of the Union;

(2)       Take decision on any urgent and important matters affecting the Union which are not
          provided for in the Constitution. Such a decision in that respect shall be binding
          provisionally on members subject to the ratification of the subsequent National
          Conference;


(3)    Take care of the Union's properties;

(4)    Represent the Union's views in all matters;

(5)    Authorize all expenditures of the Union;

(6)    Authorize promotion and discipline of Union Staff as and when the need arises;

(7)    Replace any non-performing Ex-officio member(s);

(8)    Appoint members of Standing Committees to deal with or find solution to urgent matters
       in the interest of the Union;

(9)    Appoint Ad-hoc Committees other than the Standing Committees to look into specified
       matters as the need arises;

(10)   In the absence of the National President and the National Vice President, the National
       Executive Council meeting shall be presided over by any of the vice Presidents from the
       Zones, and in their absence, any elected officer from among the members present.

(11)   Hold weekly meetings;

(12)   Hold at least 35 weekly meetings in a year and at least ten of the National Executive
       Council members shall form the quorum for the meeting.



(iii) ZONE

(1)    The recognized Zones of the Union are - Central Zone, Northern Zone, Western Zone and
       South-South Zone;

(2)    A Zone shall not be represented at the National Conference as such, as attendance is
       based on Branch representation;

(3)    Member Branches of any Zonal group shall continue to be recognized by the National
       Headquarters as individual Branches and the Zonal arrangements shall subsist and its
       decision shall be binding on Branches among themselves only.


(iv) BRANCH

(1)       Branch meetings shall be held at such time and place as such Branch agrees upon;

(2)       Each Ward in Ilorin may constitute a Branch of the Union;

(3)       Branches shall be established in all places of domicile in Nigeria and abroad where there
          are Ilorin Emirate indigenes;

(4)       Any newly formed Branch of the Union shall be required to process its registration by
          application through the Zone where it falls, to the National Executive Council. If the
          recommendation to the National Executive Council is affirmative, it shall approve the
          registration of the Branch provisionally for subsequent introduction to the National
          Conference for ratification.

(5)       The viability of a Branch shall be determined by its regular attendance, participation and
`         financial contribution at the National Conference;

(6)       Where a Branch fails to attend three (3) consecutive National Conferences and /or neglect
          to pay its annual due and Conference registration fees, such a Branch shall be deemed
          unviable and deregistered accordingly;

    (7)   Where a report of non-viability of a Branch is received by the National Executive
          Council from any Zone, whether the Branch falls within the Zone or not, such a Branch
          shall be deregistered after due investigation by the National Executive Council;

    (8)   All Branches shall send their annual dues and levies to the National Conference not later
          than the end of September of each year;

    (9)   Each Branch shall have its own Executive Committee;

(10)      There shall be 128 numbers of branches of the Union and such other number(s) as the
          congress may approve from time to time and in accordance with Section 6(iv)(4) of this
          Constitution;

(11)      The branches referred to in Sub-section (10) are those listed in the First Schedule to this
          Constitution PROVIDED that the numbers shall be added to as time and circumstances
          dictate and such new Branch shall be listed accordingly.

SECTION 7

(a) ELECTIONS

(i)     Election into the National Executive Council shall be held biennially i.e. every two years;

(ii)    On the last day of Conference of the election year, National Conference shall elect all
        officers of the National Executive Council through a majority vote of delegates and
        outgoing National Executive Council members present and voting;

(iii)   The National Executive Council as elected shall hold office for a period of two
        consecutive years;

(iv)    A National Executive Council member shall be eligible for re-election except that no
        officer can hold office for more than two consecutive terms on the same post;

(v)     The election shall be conducted by an ad-hoc Electoral Committee appointed by the
        Conference during the Conference in session;

(vi)    Election shall be by simple majority while un-opposed candidates at an election shall be
        required to have 50% yes votes to be deemed elected;

(vii)   Every member eligible to vote shall be entitled to only one vote;

(viii) Every member of the Union whether present or not at the Conference is eligible to be
        voted for; For a member to be eligible to stand for election, he must have been nominated
        and his nomination must have been seconded by accredited delegates present at the
        Conference;

(ix)    Any member of the Union who is a political office holder, either by appointment or
        election, shall not be eligible to stand for election into any office of the Union or be a
        delegate;

(x)     Election shall be conducted by secret or open ballot; Out-going Officers shall surrender all
        the Union's properties to the newly elected Officers not later than two weeks after the
        election;


(xi)    Active members shall be appointed by the elected National Executive Council as ex-
        officio members in such a way that selection shall be well spread across the Local
        Government Areas in Ilorin Emirate and professional interest groups.

(b)     BYE ELECTION

        There shall be a bye-election during the National Conference of a non-election year to fill
        any vacant elective office. Such office shall be deemed vacant in the following
        circumstances:

(i)     By resignation;

(ii)    On ground of prolonged ill health beyond six (6) months, incapacitation or death;

(iii)   Absence from meetings for six consecutive months without acceptable reason(s);

(iv)    Upon being appointed/elected into a political office;

(v)     Poor performance or persistent violation of the provision of this Constitution as may be
        determined by not less than two third (2/3) majority of the members of the National
        Executive Council present when such a decision is to be taken.

SECTION 8

COMPOSITION OF THE NATIONAL EXECUTIVE COUNCIL

The power of the Union shall be vested in a body called the National Executive Council
composed of the following Officers: -

(a)     National President;

(b)     National Vice President;

(c)     Vice President, Central Zone;

(d)     Vice President, Northern Zone;

(e)     Vice President, Western Zone;


(f)   Vice President, South-South Zone (and any other Zone so recommended by the NEC of
      the Union and approved by the National Conference);

(g)   National Secretary;

(h)   1st National Assistant Secretary, 2nd National Assistant

      Secretary and 3rd National Assistant Secretary;

(i)   National Treasurer;

(j)   National Financial Secretary;

(k)   National Assistant Financial Secretary;

(I)   National Social Secretary;

(m)   National Assistant Social Secretary;

(n)   National Publicity Secretary;

(o)   National Assistant Publicity Secretary;

(p)   National Legal Adviser;

(q)   National Internal! Auditor;

(r)   Such number of Ex Officio members as the National Executive Council may deem fit to
      appoint;

(s)   Past National Presidents, National Secretaries, current Zonal Chairmen, current Zonal
      Secretaries and current Branch Chairmen.

SECTION 10

FUNCTIONS OF THE NATIONAL EXECUTIVE OFFICERS

(a)     NATIONAL PRESIDENT

        The National President shall:

(i)     Preside over the Executive Council meetings and the National Conferences;

(ii)    Co-ordinate the activities of the National Executive Council;

(iii)   Be the Chief spokesman of the Union;

(iv)    Be the principal signatory to the Union's Bank Account(s);

 (v)    Have power to convene Emergency meetings;

(vi)    Receive monthly reports from Officers and may cause overall reports to be sent to the
        Branches when necessary;

(vii)   Perform or delegate to other Executive members those duties not treated by the
        Constitution but are in line with the aims, objectives and aspirations of the Union;

(viii) Have the power to rule, in consultation with the National Legal Adviser, on matters on
        which the Constitution is silent and which the NEC could not resolve;

(ix)    Present his action plan for his tenure within 3 months of election.



(b)     NATIONAL VICE PRESIDENT

        The National Vice President shall have power to:


(i)     Carry out the duties of the President in his absence;

(ii)    Assist the President;

(iii)   Perform other functions that may be assigned by the President or the National Executive
        Council.



(c)     VICE PRESIDENTS (ZONES)

(i)     Being members of the National Executive Council, shall carry out liaison jobs between
        the National Executive Council and the respective Zones;

(ii)    Perform other functions that may be assigned by the President or the National Executive
        Council.



(d)     NATIONAL SECRETARY

        The National Secretary shall:

(i)     Be the administrative head of the Secretariat of the Union;

(ii)    Be responsible for all the secretariat duties of the Union;

(iii)   After consultation with the President, summon the meetings of the Union;

(iv)    Record, produce and keep full and correct minutes of the Conference and Executive
        Council meetings;

(v)     Ensure the production of bounded copies of the minutes of the National Executive
        Council quarterly;

(vi)    Be responsible for preparing and reading the annual report of the Union;

(vii)   Always liaise with the President in his activities;

(viii) Be one of the alternate signatories to the Union's Bank Accounts;

(ix)    Be the overall custodian of the Union's properties;


(x)            Perform other duties assigned to him by the President or the National Executive
               Committee.

(e)            1st NATIONAL ASSISTANT SECRETARY, 2nd NATIONAL ASSISTANT
               SECRETARY AND 3rd NATIONAL ASSISTANT SECRETARY

(i)            The three (3) National Assistant Secretaries shall: Assist the National Secretary in all the
               secretariat duties and carry out the duties assigned to the Secretary in his absence;

(ii)           Perform other specific duties assigned by the Constitution;

(iii)          Perform other duties assigned by the National Secretary or the National Executive
               Council.



(f)            NATIONAL TREASURER

               The National Treasurer who shall be a professionally qualified accountant shall

        (i)       Submit annual/quarterly reports of the Union's Accounts to the National Executive
                  Council/Annual National Conference;
        (ii)      Disburse approved expenditures and keep record of same along with other financial
                  records of the Union;
        (iii)     Within 72 hours, deposit the Union's money to the Union's Bank Account(s) and
                  carry out other monetary transactions as assigned to him by the National Executive
                  Council;
        (iv)      Be one of the alternate signatories to the Union's Accounts.



(g)            NATIONAL FINANCIAL SECRETARY

               The National Financial Secretary shall:

        (i)       Collect all monies and account for same on behalf of the Union;
        (ii)      Submit all accounts and documents to the Auditor for checking when called for;
        (iii)     Collect all subscriptions from members and any money obtained from any activities
                  organized by the Union, and pay same to the Treasurer within 48 hours;


      (iv)      Issue official receipts on all monies collected;
      (v)       Keep and make available record of receipts and payments on demand;
      (vi)      Perform other duties assigned by the National Executive Council.



(j)          NATIONAL ASSISTANT FINANCIAL SECRETARY

             The National Assistant Financial Secretary shall:

      (i)       Assist the Financial Secretary in his duties;
      (ii)      Carry out all the duties assigned to the Financial Secretary in his absence;
      (iii)     Perform other duties assigned by the National Executive Council.



(k)          NATIONAL SOCIAL SECRETARY

             The National Social Secretary shall:

      (i)       Arrange activities in conjunction with Social Committee of the Union as may be
                approved by the National Executive Council;
      (ii)      See to the welfare of the delegates at the National Conference;
      (iii)     Perform other duties assigned by the National Executive Council.



(j)          NATIONAL ASSISTANT SOCIAL SECRETARY

             The National Assistant Social Secretary shall:

      (i)       Assist the National Social Secretary in his duties;
      (ii)      Carry out all the duties assigned to the Social Secretary in his absence;
      (iii)     Perform other duties assigned by the National Executive Council.



(k) NATIONAL PUBLICITY SECRETARY

             The National Publicity Secretary shall:


      (i)        Be responsible for publicizing the Union's activities in the media;
      (ii)       Perform other duties assigned by the National Executive Council.



(I)          NATIONAL ASSISTANT PUBLICITY SECRETARY

             The National Assistant Publicity Secretary shall:

      (i)        Assist the Publicity Secretary at all times;
      (ii)       Carry out all the duties assigned to the Publicity Secretary in his absence;
      (iii)      Perform other duties assigned by the National Executive Council.



(m)          NATIONAL LEGAL ADVISER

             The National Legal Adviser who shall be a Barrister and Solicitor of the Supreme Court
             of Nigeria of not less than 10 years standing at the bar shall.

      (i)        Advise the Union on ail legal matters,
      (ii)       Handle all Union's assignments involving legal issue(s);
      (iii)      Prepare all legal documents relating to the Union;
      (iv)       Have the power to interpret the rules and provisions of this Constitution,
      (v)        Perform other duties assigned by the National Executive Council.



(n)          NATIONAL INTERNAL AUDITOR

             The      National Internal Auditor who     shall    be a professionally qualified accountant
             shall:

      (i)        Be responsible for examining all the Union's Accounts with the Financial Secretary
                 and the Treasurer at least once in a year;
      (ii)       Submit a detailed report of his examination and findings to the Annual Conference;
      (iii)      Perform other duties assigned by the National Executive Council.

SECTION 11

       (a) COMPOSITION OF STANDING COMMITTEES


       (i)       General Purpose Committee;
       (ii)      Social Committee;
       (iii)     Publicity Committee;
       (iv)      Education Committee;
       (v)       Finance Committee;
       (vi)      Investment Committee;
       (vii)     Disciplinary Committee;
       (viii) Project Committee;
       (ix)      Security Committee;



(b)           FUNCTIONS OF STANDING COMMITTEES

(i)           GENERAL PURPOSE COMMITTEE

              The Committee shall:

(1)           Comprise the National President who shall be its Chairman and six (6) other members
              appointed by the National Executive Council. The Secretary to the Committee shall be
              the National Secretary;

(2)           Perform other duties assigned to it by the National Executive Council within the
              provision of this Constitution.



(ii)          SOCIAL COMMITTEE

              The Committee shall:

(1)           Comprise the Social Secretary who shall be its Chairman, Assistant Social Secretary who
              shall be the Committee's Secretary and any other five (5) members appointed by the
              National Executive Council;


(2)     Arrange all social functions including the Annual Conference as well as other activities
        of the Union;

(3)     Arrange and be responsible for transport service1 o delegates      during   the   Annual
        Conference necessary,

(4)     Perform any other social functions conferred on it by the National Executive Council
        within the provision of this Constitution.



(iii)   PUBLICITY COMMITTEE

        The Committee shall:

(1)     Comprise the Publicity Secretary as its Chairman, the Assistant Publicity Secretary as the
        Committee's Secretary and any other five (5) members appointed by the Executive
        Council;

(2)     Be responsible for the publication and distribution of the Union's Magazine, (Newsletter),
        Greeting Cards, etc.;

(3)     Produce the newsletter of the Union quarterly;

(4)     Publicize the Union's activities.



(iv)    EDUCATION COMMITTEE

        The Committee shall:

(1)     Comprise an educationist who shall be its Chairman, the 2nd National Assistant Secretary
        as the Secretary and any other five (5) members appointed by the National Executive
        Council;

(2)     Be responsible for the proper running and maintenance of the education establishments
        and projects;


(3)    Arrange public lectures and symposia for the purpose of increasing the communities'
       awareness of the importance of education;

(4)    Operate bursary/scholarship schemes for the benefit of deserving indigenes;

(5)    Compile or cause reports to be compiled on general education progress (both statistical
       and analytical) of Ilorin Emirate Community and suggest remedies for education
       problems,

(6)    Perform any other functions conferred on it by the National Executive Council in
       accordance with the provisions of this Constitution.



(v)    FINANCE COMMITTEE

       The Committee shall:

(1)    Comprise the Treasurer as the Chairman, Financial Secretary as Committee's Secretary,
       the Assistant Financial Secretary and any other two (2) member appointed by the
       National Executive Council;

(2)    Advise the Union from time to time on lawful means of raising funds;

(3)    Have a supervisory/advisory role on matters relating to the Union's revenue and
       expenditures;

(4)    Perform other functions conferred on it by the National Executive Council in accordance
       with the provisions of this Constitution.

(vi)   INVESTMENT COMMITTEE

       The Committee shall:

(1)    Comprise a management expert as its Chairman, the 3rd National Assistant Secretary
       as   the Secretary, Treasurer, Financial Secretary, Legal Adviser and any other two (2)
       nominees;

(2)    Advise the Union from time to time on the most profitable means of investing its funds;
(3)    Oversee all investment and business ventures of the Union;


(4)     Keep ail the records of the Union's investments;

(5)     Remit the proceeds profits from all investments to the Union

(6)     Perform any other functions assigned to it by the National Executive Council.



(vii)   DISCIPLINARY COMMITTEE

        The Committee shall:

(1)     Comprise the National Vice President as the Chairman Legal Adviser and any other three
        members appointed by the National Executive Council.

(2)     instill discipline in members by enforcing strict compliance with the provisions of this
        Constitution;

(3)     Ensure accurate judgment within the scope of this Constitution;

(4)     Consider all cases of offence referred to it by the National Executive Council recommend
        appropriate disciplinary action to be melted out to the offender;

(5)     Have the power to hear complain of a member, Branch or Zone who wishes to appeal any
        case;

(6)     Have power over staff disciplinary matters referred to it by the National Executive
        Council;

(7)     Submit its written recommendation(s) on all cases to the National Executive Council
        which shall have the power to approve or reject the recommendation. However, any
        disciplinary action involving the expulsion of a member of the union must be submitted
        to the National Conference for ratification.



(viii) PROJECT COMMITTEE

           The Committee shall:


       (1) Comprise a management expert as the Chairman and any other four members appointed
              by the National Executive Council,
       (2) Serve in advisory role from time to time on projects to be executed by the Union;
       (3) Oversee the projects of the Union as assigned by the National Executive Council;
       (4) Ensure prudent management and execution of the Union's project;
       (5) Perform other functions assigned to it by the National Executive Council




(ix)          SECURITY COMMITTEE

              The Committee shall:

       (1) Comprise a security expert who shall be its Chapman and any other four members
              appointed by the National Executive Council,
       (2) Be responsible for creating security awareness amongst members of the Union and the
              general public:
       (3) Have a supervisory/advisory role on matters relating to security and safety of life and
              property;
       (4) Liaise with the Security Agencies on provision of adequate security for delegates at the
              National Conference and other activities organized by the Union;
       (5) Perform other functions assigned to it by the National Executive Council.

SECTION 13

FINANCE

(a)     FUNDS

        The following shall be the main sources of funds of the Union:

(i)     Monthly dues, the amount to be determined by member of the respective Branches;

(ii)    Levy may be imposed by the Branches on each member and by the National
        Headquarters on the Branches;

(iii)   Borrowing from members or from the Union's Bankers;

(iv)    Donations from members or other well-wishers;

(v)     Sales of books or publications and revenue from disposal of the property of the Union
        with the authority of the National Executive Council;

(vi)    Public Elections and donations from the general Public for specific purpose from time to
        time;

(vii)   Proceeds of economic and social activities of the Union;

(viii) income from any commercial venture of the Union;

(ix)    Annual dues from member Branches and any other money mat the Branches may deem
        necessary to be emitted :o the National Headquarters;

(x)     Any other awful means of generating revenue.

(b) ACCOUNTS

(i)     Receipts must be issued for ai! monies received on behalf of the Union;

(ii)    AH monies belonging to the Union must be deposited in the Union s account within 48
        hours of receipt;

(iii)   Any member of the Union who collects any money for or from the Union would be
        expected to give acceptable accounts of such collections;


(iv)    Proper records must be kept for all monies received ana disbursed by the Union;

(v)     An annual! account of all financial transactions of the Union must be prepared by the
        Treasurer and Financial Secretary and checked by the Auditor.



(c) AUDIT

(i)     An external Auditor who shall be a member of a recognized Accounting Body may be
        invited to audit the account of the Union when necessary irrespective of whether or not
        the accounts were checked by the Internal Auditor;

(ii)    The report on observations and recommendations of such external auditing exercise shall
        be received by the National Executive Council for discussion and subsequent
        presentation to the National Conference for implementation.

SECTION 14

TRUSTEES

(a)     His Royal Highness, the Emir of Horn- shall of the lite Patron of the Union and shall be
        one of the registered Trustees;

(b)     The Trustees for the Union, for the purpose of Companies and Allied Matters Act 1990
        shall he appointed at the Annual National Conference of the Union by a simple majority
        of members present;

(c)     Such registered Trustees shall be seven (7) in number and shall be known as the
        Registered Trustees of florin Emirate Descendants Progressive Union (I.E.D.P.U);

(d)     A Trustee shall cease to hold office if he:

(i)     Resigns his office;

(ii)    Becomes insane;

(iii)   Is officially declared bankrupt;


(iv)    Is dead

(v)     Is recommended for removal from office by two-third (2/3) votes of members at the
        National Conference of the Union.

(e)     Upon a vacancy occurring in the membership of the Trustees, a subsequent National
        Conference shall appoint an eligible member in replacement;

(f)     The common sea! of the Trustees shall be kept in the custody of the National Secretary
        who shall produce it when required for use by the Trustees;

(g)     The Trustee shall have a common seal;

(h)     All documents to be executed by the Trustees shall be signed by any 5 or the Registered
        Trustees and sealed by common seal;

(i)     The Trustees shall apply to the Corporate Affairs Commission for Certificate of
        Incorporation under the Companies and Allied Matters Act No. 1. of 1990-part C;

(j)     If such Certificate is granted, the Trustees shall have power to accept and hoses in bust all
        land belonging to Ilorin Emirate Descendants Progressive Union (I.E.D.P.U) and to
        acquire landed properties, equipment and other materials on behalf of (I.E.D.P.U) subject
        to such condition as the Commission may impose.

SECTION 15

(a)     STAFF OF THE UNION

(i)     The National Executive Council shall set up Employment Committee to be chaired by the
        National Secretary to handle Union staff recruitment, discipline and promotion as the
        need arises;

(ii)    Suitable members and non-members of the Union shall be eligible for appointment as
        staff of the Union;

(iii)   All employees of the Union shall hold office at the pleasure of the Union;


(iv)    Union staff in the performance of their duties shall be under the general supervisions of
        the National Secretary;

(v)     Any staff of the Union may resign his/her appointment at any time by fulfilling the terms
        and conditions of his/her appointment;

(vi)    The staff of the Union shall be required to give at least one month notice to the National
        Secretary or pay one month's salary in lieu of notice after which the resignation shall
        become effective;

(vii)   A resigning Union staff shall be required to surrender all properties of the Union in
        his/her custody to the National Secretary and shall settle any debt which may be
        outstanding against his/her name.

(b)     PROPERTY OF THE UNION

(i)     Anything belonging to the Union is regarded as the Union Property;

(ii)    Individual Officer shall be accountable for property assigned to his office;

(iii)   Union Property shall not be put to private use and as much as practicable shall be at the
        Union Secretariat;

(iv)    Major repairs of the Union Property shall be undertaken only with the consent of the
        National Executive Council;

(v)     Repair shall be deemed major when above N10,000.00.
